From: rknpu-rk3588 project <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] iommu: report the real IOMMU runtime PM state in rockchip_iommu_is_enabled()

rknpu_power_off() polls rockchip_iommu_is_enabled() until the IOMMU is
disabled before powering down the NPU1/NPU2 domains, because the IOMMU
runtime suspend (rk_iommu_disable(), which touches the MMU registers of
every core) runs asynchronously once the NPU, its PM device-link
consumer, is suspended.

The compat stub returned true whenever the device had an IOMMU group,
i.e. always in IOMMU mode: every power-off then timed out ("iommu still
enabled"), re-took the runtime PM reference and left the NPU powered.

Resolve the "iommus" phandle to the IOMMU platform device and report
whether it is still runtime-active (not RPM_SUSPENDED), which is what
the vendor helper reports with its own enable state. No change in
non-IOMMU mode: without an available IOMMU node it returns false, as
before.

Tested on Radxa ROCK 5B (RK3588), Armbian 7.3.4-edge-rockchip64.

--- a/src/include/compat/soc/rockchip/rockchip_iommu.h
+++ b/src/include/compat/soc/rockchip/rockchip_iommu.h
@@ -6,16 +6,38 @@
 
 #include <linux/device.h>
 #include <linux/iommu.h>
+#include <linux/of.h>
+#include <linux/of_platform.h>
+#include <linux/platform_device.h>
+#include <linux/pm_runtime.h>
 
+/*
+ * rknpu_power_off() polls this until the IOMMU is really disabled before
+ * powering down the NPU1/NPU2 domains: the IOMMU runtime suspend (supplier
+ * of the NPU through a PM device link) runs asynchronously and touches the
+ * MMU registers of every core. Report whether the IOMMU device referenced by
+ * "iommus" is still runtime-active (not RPM_SUSPENDED), like the vendor
+ * rockchip_iommu_is_enabled() does with its enable state.
+ */
 static inline bool rockchip_iommu_is_enabled(struct device *dev)
 {
-	/* If the device has an IOMMU group, IOMMU is enabled */
-	struct iommu_group *group = iommu_group_get(dev);
-	if (group) {
-		iommu_group_put(group);
-		return true;
-	}
-	return false;
+	struct device_node *np;
+	struct platform_device *pdev;
+	bool active;
+
+	np = of_parse_phandle(dev->of_node, "iommus", 0);
+	if (!np)
+		return false;
+
+	pdev = of_find_device_by_node(np);
+	of_node_put(np);
+	if (!pdev)
+		return false;
+
+	active = !pm_runtime_status_suspended(&pdev->dev);
+	put_device(&pdev->dev);
+
+	return active;
 }
 
 static inline void rockchip_iommu_disable(struct device *dev)
